From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 07:43:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: declare stack_scan_from before RaiseException
 uses it.

The C++ throw diagnostic calls it a hundred lines above the definition, so
the compiler saw an implicit -- and therefore non-static -- declaration
first and the real one collided with it.  The 64-bit build never showed
this because it was incremental and did not recompile the file; a clean
32-bit build fails outright.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit c552690110f77db07f0cff04fd409b256aa3cd21)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
index a83dd8c2a9a..a3466220ce4 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
@@ -42,6 +42,12 @@ WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(seh);
 WINE_DECLARE_DEBUG_CHANNEL(winedbg);
 WINE_DECLARE_DEBUG_CHANNEL(cxxthrow);
 
+
+/* Defined further down, next to the comment explaining what it is for; declared
+ * here because the C++ throw diagnostic in RaiseException() uses it first.
+ * Without this the 32-bit build fails: the implicit declaration is non-static
+ * and collides with the real one. */
+static void stack_scan_from( const ULONG_PTR *sp, const char *what );
 typedef INT (WINAPI *MessageBoxA_funcptr)(HWND,LPCSTR,LPCSTR,UINT);
 typedef INT (WINAPI *MessageBoxW_funcptr)(HWND,LPCWSTR,LPCWSTR,UINT);
 
